cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ledgerline: a Java 25 vs .NET 10 benchmark on a realistic backend workload"
message: "If you quote a number from this benchmark, please cite it and say which run it came from."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Asatryan
    given-names: Haik
repository-code: "https://github.com/HaikAsatryan/java-vs-dotnet-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  The same invoicing API, specified once in a frozen spec/ and implemented twice, in Java
  25 LTS (Spring Boot 4, WebMVC on virtual threads, Spring Data JPA and Hibernate 7) and
  .NET 10 (Minimal API, EF Core 10), against a shared PostgreSQL 18.4 and Redis. The
  measured quantity is cost at a fixed latency promise: CPU-ms and steady-state memory per
  request at the rate where each stack's own mixed-workload p99 crosses 20 ms, read from
  cgroup v2. Load is open-loop and coordinated-omission-safe. The published run is
  full-20260827T174611-fedora, config hash
  e9fef8d3abbba8db034084d6295d3169a302a10a14ee1a13bc0d94b431fa3166.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - java
  - dotnet
  - performance
  - postgresql
  - cgroups
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-12"
